SUMMARY
==============================================================================
NR-D1: REPRODUCED (2/2) — exact time-reversal mirror; reversed state runs an anti-arrow to S = 0
NR-D3: REPRODUCED (2/2) — same marginals: correlated state recoheres to purity, product-of-marginals does not (max-mixed-ish bath)
NR-D4: REPRODUCED (2/2) — fresh maximally mixed bath: Markovian contraction, entropy rise, records; correlated bath: non-monotone
NR-D5: REPRODUCED (3/3) — bath reuse destroys monotone (semigroup) behaviour; single reused ancilla re-purifies
NR-D7: REPRODUCED (2/2) — records form forward (0 -> >=5) and un-form from the reversed state (>=5 -> 0)
NR-D8: REPRODUCED (1/1) — same global state: product/rising in one TPS, flat high-entropy in another
NR-D2: REPRODUCED (2/2) — typicality: P(increase) ~ 1/2, states already near maximal
